  "unsafe_boundary": {
    "type": "private trames_vulkan::context::OwnedBackend only",
    "invariants": [
      "Backend and its Rc/RefCell objects remain !Send/!Sync; no blanket implementation. Context consumes an entire private graph with no escaping Rc/Object/borrow in its public API.",
      "The Context mutex serializes all graph entry, movement and final teardown. Independent Context objects use independent mutexes. No guest Memory/View or page guard is stored in the graph.",
      "Existing compiler workers only receive Send-owned parameters/native handles/Arc<Device>; Rc dependencies remain in the backend graph. UI frames contain Arc native-image/device/fence leases, no backend Rc. Display/Server/Budget are already Send/Sync.",
      "Future API that leaks graph aliases, retains stack pointers/TLS-affine data or reenters a context requires a new audit. This boundary does not claim individual object concurrency."
    ]
  },
  "corrections": [
    "First check --tests found five test-only Work constructors missing the new optional GPU field; supplied None. Production and all affected test targets subsequently check/build successfully.",
    "New GPU budget test initially expected no remaining credit even for invalid function. Original behavior faults before retiring/reserving HLT, leaving one credit. Test-only expectation corrected; four scenarios pass.",
    "First strict Clippy rejected assert_eq with a literal bool in the new memory test. Changed only that assertion to assert; final strict Clippy passed.",
    "copyfile omitted executable mode on saved baseline; first integration failed before running a sample. Restored local executable bit, kept identical baseline content hash; final 24 comparisons passed.",
    "First host render command missed the required output PPM argument and failed its argc assertion. Corrected only the command; guest/host render outputs and image bytes match."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Linux x86_64 Mesa lavapipe software Vulkan driver only; no new Apple/MoltenVK, real GPU, iPad UI or zero-copy presentation acceptance.",
    "Same-context mutex contention can block a host worker. Per-object/queue GPU parallelism and parking lock contention are not implemented by this batch.",
    "Async pipeline compile start/completion, device/instance teardown and Wayland FD authentication remain owner/joined. Native Wayland relay pumping and other external host I/O retain their original boundary. No new poller or service thread.",
    "Fixed 32 GPU operations and 1024 1 MiB native fills per integration sample. Fence-status query counts can vary with native completion. Structural counters only, no statistical timing/application speed claims.",
    "Original standard render peer ends before draws, so its worker_gpu_calls=0. Wrapped render holds a condition-variable peer throughout the unchanged main, achieves 109 worker GPU calls and exact same oracle image.",
    "No broad CPU/Linux/VFS/network/GPU application suites, CoreMark/Docker/Firefox reruns, QEMU, Apple 16 KiB pages, or IPA/release. No private Firefox diagnostics read or archived."
  ],
